    "updated_at": "2019-12-09T12:53:06Z",
    "body": "I realized that in Chrome it's possible for an `iframe` element to be connected and not have a nested browsing context (since that is created when `load` is dispatched, which is post-insertion; observable through inserting multiple `iframe` elements or with a `script` element), but this is a condition the HTML Standard already accounts for in its various accessors.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/19693 has more tests/assertions for those now. It's also a little weird that sometimes a nested browsing context is created with an event and sometimes without.",
