    "body": "@stephenmcgruer the title of https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1598674 says \"Hundreds of timeouts\" so maybe just summarizing the results (e.g. \"Firefox: 103 new tests, 103 timeout\") would bring attention to it where that's surprising.\r\n\r\nI'm struggling to find a single wpt PR that added the tests, https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/4292 is the oldest but https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/4292#issuecomment-265404720 actually looks good.\r\n\r\nHuge numbers of timeouts will make the tests run slower and can often be turned into a fast fail, but it's not a case that I think we can require any action for when the tests are new as here. Regressing to timeout is a different matter and probably worth flagging.",
